    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update jaero to 1.0.4.14

DEPENDENCY / STAGING ORDER: this request needs the new qmqtt package,
submitted separately as SR 1373859 (hardware:sdr/qmqtt -&gt;
openSUSE:Factory). qmqtt must be accepted FIRST, or staged together with
this request; jaero 1.0.4.14 cannot build without it. jaero builds
against the qt5 flavour, so it needs qmqtt-qt5-devel from that package.

Upstream 1.0.4.14 adds an MQTT client (subscribe to and publish decoded
ACARS messages over a broker, with TLS and authentication), reworks input
handling into a dedicated feeder dialog, adds a JSONdump output format
mimicking dumpvdl2/dumphfdl, and fixes a source/destination mix-up, the
ZMQ checkbox having no effect and duplicate burst-data deliveries. It
also moves from libacars 1 to libacars 2.

ALSO FIXES A LIVE BREAKAGE: jaero currently fails to build on Leap 16.0
(aarch64, ppc64le and x86_64) with &quot;cannot find -lqcustomplot&quot;, because
jaero-fix-build-with-qcustomplot-qt5.patch was gated on
suse_version &gt; 1600, which excludes 16.0 itself. That patch is now
applied unconditionally, repairing those three architectures.

Two patches are involved: jaero-fix-build-with-qcustomplot-qt5.patch
(kept, refreshed, now unconditional) and jaero-use-system-qmqtt.patch
(new, links the system qmqtt shared library instead of the in-tree qmake
module upstream expects to build itself).

Packaging cleanup: the bundled JFFT source is pinned to the commit
upstream builds against rather than a floating master branch archive
(contents unchanged), the package now ships its own jaero.desktop instead
of using the deprecated %suse_update_desktop_file macro, the Group tag is
gone, the tarball is named .tar.gz to match what GitHub serves, and
%make_jobs is replaced by %make_build.

Built and verified natively on aarch64 (openSUSE_Tumbleweed): rpmlint
clean, 0 errors, 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1373860</requestid>
